[[:db/retract 17592186363726 :question/answer-fields 17592186363727] {:db/id 17592186229185 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-abc3945b-d976-54fe-bc38-a631f9c8a6c5" "question-11008462-bb8d-5c30-9ab6-4b789c8f149b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-abc3945b-d976-54fe-bc38-a631f9c8a6c5" :question/id #uuid "abc3945b-d976-54fe-bc38-a631f9c8a6c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-332291" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-4y=8.\n$$\n\nFind the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The right-hand side of our inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}(x)=0.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0-4\\alpha =8\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e5c92c86-227c-5c65-bc14-31ff63640148"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e5c92c86-227c-5c65-bc14-31ff63640148" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5c92c86-227c-5c65-bc14-31ff63640148" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-79ad64d0-e59a-5622-ad8f-a7d521d9e58a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-79ad64d0-e59a-5622-ad8f-a7d521d9e58a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79ad64d0-e59a-5622-ad8f-a7d521d9e58a" :answer/id #uuid "79ad64d0-e59a-5622-ad8f-a7d521d9e58a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-11008462-bb8d-5c30-9ab6-4b789c8f149b" :question/id #uuid "11008462-bb8d-5c30-9ab6-4b789c8f149b" :question/math-academy-id "q-332303" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y=12x-8.\n$$\n\nFind the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\alpha -6(\\alpha x+\\beta )=12x-8\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-6\\alpha x+(\\alpha -6\\beta )=12x-8.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-6\\alpha =12\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\alpha -6\\beta =-8\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-2,\\,\\beta =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2x+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fc1fdf7c-1bca-53aa-87e0-8b914a783aff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fc1fdf7c-1bca-53aa-87e0-8b914a783aff" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc1fdf7c-1bca-53aa-87e0-8b914a783aff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fcf2db36-4823-5f0f-a979-18eb641ef853" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fcf2db36-4823-5f0f-a979-18eb641ef853"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcf2db36-4823-5f0f-a979-18eb641ef853" :answer/id #uuid "fcf2db36-4823-5f0f-a979-18eb641ef853" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229186 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-927f3245-f67b-58d6-852d-475c4b37e55f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186363726 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ea7da04c-6c47-53af-93ba-6b58aa8bcba5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea7da04c-6c47-53af-93ba-6b58aa8bcba5" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea7da04c-6c47-53af-93ba-6b58aa8bcba5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a813be27-9e89-5447-a6ed-ccb753aec0ff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a813be27-9e89-5447-a6ed-ccb753aec0ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a813be27-9e89-5447-a6ed-ccb753aec0ff" :answer/id #uuid "a813be27-9e89-5447-a6ed-ccb753aec0ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Ae^{-6x}+2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-927f3245-f67b-58d6-852d-475c4b37e55f" :question/id #uuid "927f3245-f67b-58d6-852d-475c4b37e55f" :question/math-academy-id "q-332544" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=-8.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-4x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\beta $ is a constant to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0+4\\beta =-8\n$$\n\nSolving this equation gives $\\beta =-2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e554faf-bf14-5f8b-8095-42b409f87077"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e554faf-bf14-5f8b-8095-42b409f87077" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e554faf-bf14-5f8b-8095-42b409f87077" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-447d61bd-85be-5a77-92c7-e7b1cbcac24d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-447d61bd-85be-5a77-92c7-e7b1cbcac24d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-447d61bd-85be-5a77-92c7-e7b1cbcac24d" :answer/id #uuid "447d61bd-85be-5a77-92c7-e7b1cbcac24d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{-4x}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-0aa93e49-72e3-5515-b5a3-3f4b53ceca51" :activity/id #uuid "0aa93e49-72e3-5515-b5a3-3f4b53ceca51" :activity/title "General Solutions of First-Order Linear ODEs" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049370 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-5fac2716-ce9b-5cad-acde-41963ce110a0" "step-e7fb33d5-37b5-560d-9083-478d43405b96" "step-2c1d4d31-bdd3-5e06-8ac4-128b5af0e137" "step-19ee83f6-1de2-5260-a0ac-12e506110b20" "step-218a75cb-ded3-56d6-8e5a-f6b0268721ec"] :activity/first-step "step-5fac2716-ce9b-5cad-acde-41963ce110a0" :db/ensure [:activi